# The compiler binary, built from the checked-in seed by bootstrap/build.sh.
#
# ⚠️ Only the BINARY.  bootstrap/*.c and bootstrap/*.h are the seed itself and
# must stay in the repository -- they are the only way into the language, since
# the compiler is written in Algol-24 and compiles itself.
bootstrap/algc

# Emitted C: the default --compile output directory, and anything a harness
# writes beside it.
out/
build/

# The specification rendered for printing.
#
# ⚠️ A GENERATED artifact, and it goes stale the moment ALGOL-24.md changes --
# silently, because nothing compares the two.  That is the same failure the
# corpus is built to avoid (see conformance/README.md), just slower: a file that
# looks authoritative and agrees with nothing.  The one that was tracked
# predated the conformance pass and still claimed 248 rules all awaiting a
# conformance program.
#
# Regenerate from ALGOL-24.md when a copy on paper is wanted.
spec/ALGOL-24.pdf

# macOS
.DS_Store

# The conformance corpus is GENERATED from the specification.
#
# ⚠️ Every case lives in spec/ALGOL-24.md, printed under the rule it pins as its
# program and the shell output it produces.  ./conform.sh writes these files out
# and runs them, so editing one here edits a build artifact and the next run
# overwrites it.  Change the case in the specification.
#
# The module fixtures a case imports are NOT generated and stay tracked.
conformance/*.a24
conformance/*.out
conformance/*.args
refusals/*.a24
refusals/*.expected
refusals/*.args
!conformance/modules/
